WEBVTT

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:29.830
Thanks for waiting.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:34.280
Peperoncino is ready.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:38.050
Luke, how many times do I have to tell you 
to keep that away from me?

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.530
It's good.

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:41.810
Vlad, you should try it sometime.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:47.370
The aroma of olive oil and chili peppers
 will whet your appetite.

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:49.980
Thanks for the meal.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.450
I can't make good tea
 when this place stinks of garlic.

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:55.120
I'm out of here.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:57.200
But we just opened!

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.710
Thank you.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:05.080
Sorry. Excuse me.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:18.250
Who are you?

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:20.000
What are you doing in here?

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:18.670
Mirror, mirror on the wall...

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:22.530
<i>Take the Piccadilly line 
for King's Cross Station.</i>

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:24.840
It answered my question before I could ask.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:28.750
How does this thing predict 
what I'm going to say?

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:30.210
Thanks for waiting.

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:33.110
We're free, Shinyao! Free!

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:34.960
We're in a new world!

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:36.710
It's always been your dream, Ton.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.050
Since the moment I was born.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:42.400
But we're still at the airport.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.640
Don't get too carried away yet.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:48.080
There aren't any double-decker buses,
 palaces, or cathedrals here.

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:54.930
Today we'll move into our apartment.

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:59.030
Tomorrow we'll buy basic necessities 
and register for school.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:03.400
There's only two weeks until the 
entrance ceremony, so we'll be busy, but...

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:04.870
Ton?

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:10.290
This is London,
 the city my great-grandmother loved.

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:15.530
You've loved your great-grandmother 
since you were a child.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:22.340
Thank you so much, Shinyao.

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:23.930
Where did that come from?

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:28.060
If you hadn't recognized my potential 
and pushed me in the right direction,

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:31.230
I never would've studied abroad.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:35.600
But if you hadn't declared you'd 
study abroad no matter what,

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:37.780
I never would have thought 
about leaving the country.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:40.190
I only brought it up.

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:42.100
You handled all the details.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:45.160
But I couldn't take that first step.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:48.370
But I, uh...

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:52.810
Ton, you take me to unknown worlds.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:53.830
You give me courage.

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:56.020
You're my friend for life.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:58.290
I feel the same way.

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:09.130
Wow, it's London!

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:11.930
Yeah, it really is London.

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:16.830
Everything's so old-fashioned and cool!

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:24.710
Let's start by heading to our apartment.

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:25.840
It's this way.

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:27.300
I'll take this.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:28.710
You don't need to do that.

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:30.410
It must be heavy.

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:31.370
Not really.

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:35.370
Anyway, you can show me the way.

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:37.590
Okay.

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:52.240
I think we turn right down that street.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:53.810
We're almost there.

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:56.370
I'm hungry.

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:58.020
We've walked pretty far.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:02.230
Who said I just needed to show her the way?

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:07.340
I'm hungry, too.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:08.450
Right?

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:13.700
No way...

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:16.270
Our luggage disappeared.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:17.900
No, we've been robbed!

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:20.980
What? But I didn't see anything.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:22.970
There he is!

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:24.840
Hold it right there, thief!

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:26.510
Wait, Ton!

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:29.320
Our passports, credit cards, and phones!

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:31.720
Ton, let's go to the police!

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:34.360
And my great-grandmother's keepsake!

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:38.230
Ton!

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:41.520
Someone catch him!

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:42.800
Thief!

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:46.460
Why isn't anyone helping?

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:48.450
I thought this was a country of gentlemen!

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:55.450
As always, thank you for your patronage.

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:57.220
I'll stop by again sometime.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:09.420
How uncivilized to disrupt human society.

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:10.760
Wait!

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:12.660
Thief!

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:17.100
Now this brings back memories.

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:27.160
Where am I?

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:28.320
Shinyao?

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:35.410
I know. That spell...

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:42.330
I think this is what it looked like.

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:48.250
Yeah.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:54.780
Guidance of the sun and moon, come to me.

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:14.990
This is the sixth time.

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:18.320
Thank you.

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:20.870
Oh, no.

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:23.460
Sorry. Excuse me.

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:37.100
Who are you?

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:40.530
What are you doing in here?

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:43.650
No, wait. How were you able to enter?

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:45.650
Well, uh...

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:48.110
I was led here by a magic spell.

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:50.690
Wait, isn't this a cafe?

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:53.360
There shouldn't be anything wrong 
with a customer entering a cafe.

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:55.070
That's not what I meant.

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:58.610
That spot where you're standing is...

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:00.250
Could it be?

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:08.250
Rijan's alive.

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:15.010
Chop!

00:09:17.350 --> 00:09:21.450
Vlad, decide if you're interrogating her
 or seducing her!

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.220
Not that you should be doing either!

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:24.670
You're wrong! I—

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:25.650
E-Excuse me...

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:33.530
We've been waiting for you, 
descendant of Sha Rijan-sama.

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:36.150
Huh? What?

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:49.080
You're closing early again today?

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:50.730
Come again.

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:52.790
Baileu Ton?

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:53.440
Yeah.

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:56.650
Sha Rijan's my great-grandmother.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:57.990
Seriously?

00:09:58.350 --> 00:09:59.520
Her great-granddaughter.

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:02.370
I see. It's been so long already.

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:06.210
You've met my great-grandmother?

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:08.830
But she passed away almost 
a hundred years ago.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:13.030
Yeah. I couldn't protect her back th—

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:17.320
She's legendary at this cafe.

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:19.550
After all, she was the first owner.

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:20.420
What?

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:23.540
This is Cafe Forbidden.

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:28.520
Your great-grandmother opened 
this cafe so misfits like us

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:31.450
from all over London could work here.

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:33.710
So that's why that spell brought me here.

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:37.340
It's real.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:41.300
My great-grandmother was protecting me.

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:43.540
She led me here.

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:47.700
Of course.

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:49.890
Her power that remains here is still—

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:51.540
Nice to meet you, miss.

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:53.290
This is Vlad.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:56.250
He's a lazy guy who can't 
do anything except make tea.

00:10:57.740 --> 00:11:00.970
That's Toryu. He's from your country.

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:04.560
He's a bit large for a waiter, 
but don't let it bother you.

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:07.440
And I'm Luke.

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:10.750
I'm a super chef and the 
backbone of this cafe.

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:11.980
Don't forget it.

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:16.340
So, I ran into a thief earlier...

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:19.700
Robbed the moment you arrived, huh?

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:22.160
Sounds rough.

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:23.510
It was.

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:27.120
While chasing after him,
 I got separated from my friend.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:29.820
So, what'd he look like?

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:32.900
Age, sex, build, whatever.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:34.790
Tell us everything you remember.

00:11:36.230 --> 00:11:38.300
It's actually a bit strange.

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:39.760
Strange how?

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:44.860
He was kind of blurry and fuzzy.

00:11:44.860 --> 00:11:47.220
He simultaneously seemed like one and many.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:51.600
Sorry. You must not know 
what I'm talking about.

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:53.560
I see. I know exactly who you mean.

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:55.770
What? From that?

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:58.730
See? It's our turn to shine.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:01.700
Don't act so self-important. 
It's just a coincidence.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:06.410
You think it's a coincidence 
she got behind the mirror, too?

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:09.370
Rijan-sama must have led her here.

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:12.080
Um, excuse me.

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:14.540
Which way did he run?

00:12:16.010 --> 00:12:19.550
I lost sight of him around Chinatown.

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:21.570
Chinatown. That's west of here.

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:23.690
Based on his actions, 
he sounds like a goblin.

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:27.930
The city becomes infested with them 
every year around this time.

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:31.840
If he's a goblin, he must 
have a den invisible to human eyes

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:34.230
where he keeps his  stolen treasure.

00:12:34.740 --> 00:12:38.820
Normally they use caves 
or clearings in forests.

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:40.830
In other words, someplace outdoors.

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:42.530
In a city, that'd be a park.

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:46.240
Additionally, the park west of here is...

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:47.200
Hey!

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:48.530
Hyde Park.

00:12:49.110 --> 00:12:50.490
What about the cafe?

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:51.430
Don't worry.

00:12:51.430 --> 00:12:52.540
There's one more of us here.

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:55.120
What? Hey!

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:56.500
Don't leave me here!

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.420
And tell me what's going on!

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:02.090
Huh? Where'd they go?

00:13:03.150 --> 00:13:05.170
Did they say Hyde Park?

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:14.180
Keep the change.

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:16.150
This is a park?

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:24.560
Where are they?

00:13:24.890 --> 00:13:26.660
Is something wrong?

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:29.700
Sorry for scaring you.

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:33.590
Since you were wandering around here 
alone in the middle of the night,

00:13:33.590 --> 00:13:35.100
I couldn't help but wonder.

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:38.620
Oh, no. I'm sorry.

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:40.960
I'm looking for someone.

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:46.380
Are you looking for three young men?

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:47.680
You've seen them?

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:49.980
Yes, about ten minutes ago.

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:53.140
They entered the woods just over there.

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:54.870
Thank you, sir.

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:55.810
See you later.

00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:57.310
Hold on.

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:02.210
You dropped something, miss.

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:05.950
But... this was stolen from me this evening.

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:09.660
It slipped out of your pocket just now.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:11.870
Was I confused?

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:14.640
People make assumptions all the time.

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:16.120
Don't worry about it.

00:14:16.490 --> 00:14:19.580
Make sure you wear it so 
you don't lose it again.

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:21.630
I'm sure it will be useful.

00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:24.380
Thank you.

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:26.400
I'd better get going.

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:30.610
See? Useful already.

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:38.660
Why don't you show yourself already?

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.780
If he won't answer, we have no choice.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.780
What is this?

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:56.160
A monster!

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:57.870
So it is a goblin.

00:14:58.350 --> 00:15:01.540
The quintessential savage 
and uncivilized small fry.

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:05.550
But because of it,
 they're easily recognizable.

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:08.260
Every time you defeat one, 
there's another to take its place.

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:13.800
Fools who cause mischief 
without any purpose or goal.

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:18.530
If you abandon that treasure and leave,

00:15:18.530 --> 00:15:20.770
I'll destroy you painlessly.

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:25.130
Vlad, he seems to be new.

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:26.480
He doesn't understand you.

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:31.610
Whoops.

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:34.000
Unbelievable.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:38.200
Youngsters these days have no manners at all.

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:41.710
What am I looking at?

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:44.910
What should we do?

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:47.470
The ones we see now aren't all of them.

00:15:47.470 --> 00:15:49.240
Yeah, I smell them.

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:51.050
Handle them.

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:53.720
You idiots can play together.

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:55.350
He vanished?

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:58.100
You just can't be bothered 
to fight hand-to-hand!

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:00.600
Bastards!

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:04.440
Luke-san?

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:10.470
Toryu!

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:12.940
That's too much! It's overkill!

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:17.570
Okay!

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:24.080
What is this?

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:25.540
This is too much!

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:41.170
I see.

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:44.980
You've decided to show yourself.

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:48.160
Spriggan, guardian of treasures.

00:16:49.280 --> 00:16:50.150
Look out behind you!

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:52.740
Vlad-san!

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:54.860
How did you get in here?

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:55.700
What?

00:16:55.930 --> 00:16:58.530
I told you to watch out. Why didn't you move?

00:16:58.770 --> 00:17:01.910
Because you suddenly appeared. 
You distracted me.

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:05.040
Wait. What do you think you're doing?

00:17:05.350 --> 00:17:07.960
I'll distract it while you run.

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:18.050
Ton-sama.

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:19.350
Stop!

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:20.670
Run, miss!

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:21.810
Leave him!

00:17:22.030 --> 00:17:24.690
He's badly injured. I can't do that.

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:26.520
Wait. Look at me.

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:29.770
See? I'm fine.

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:34.600
Stop!

00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:35.280
Bastard!

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:37.280
Huh?

00:17:37.630 --> 00:17:38.890
What are these?

00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:41.790
Chains?

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:46.720
What do you think you're doing, Rijan?

00:17:48.140 --> 00:17:50.420
What should I do? What's going on?

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:51.820
Do what you want.

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:54.550
They'll obviously protect you.

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:58.930
How can you say that when 
I'm clearly in trouble?

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:03.140
That's Rijan-sama's...

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:04.930
You can't be serious.

00:18:09.820 --> 00:18:11.070
Baileu Ton.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:12.150
What?

00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:14.590
Don't move a muscle!

00:18:37.520 --> 00:18:40.750
This must be your suitcase, right?

00:18:40.750 --> 00:18:42.220
It smells like you.

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:44.890
What was that?

00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:48.250
Who are you?

00:18:48.720 --> 00:18:51.120
And what am I?

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:51.750
Ton.

00:18:53.870 --> 00:18:56.820
Listen to me.

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:01.630
Today you arrived in London.

00:19:01.630 --> 00:19:03.660
Some thieves stole your luggage.

00:19:17.220 --> 00:19:19.480
Huh? I...

00:19:22.810 --> 00:19:24.930
Last night was crazy.

00:19:31.460 --> 00:19:32.370
Shinyao?

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:33.150
<i>Ton!</i>

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:35.200
<i>Where have you been?</i>

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:36.820
I finally got hold of you.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:39.400
Are you at the apartment? 
Did you already move in?

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:41.080
<i>Forget that. Are you okay?</i>

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:43.780
<i>Are you hurt? You must be hungry.</i>

00:19:44.010 --> 00:19:47.410
You don't need to be so worried. I'm great.

00:19:47.860 --> 00:19:48.930
<i>Really?</i>

00:19:48.930 --> 00:19:52.450
Oh, but a bunch of crazy 
stuff happened after that.

00:19:52.450 --> 00:19:55.630
The police got involved. 
There was a huge chase.

00:20:03.370 --> 00:20:07.350
Hey, guys. Did we really do the right thing?

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:09.530
She's not Rijan.

00:20:10.280 --> 00:20:11.850
She's just a student.

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:15.020
If this is what Ton-sama wants...

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:19.010
But it's not what she wants.

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:21.650
She just fells for his charms 
and had her memories erased.

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:28.080
Even so, Rijan wouldn't have wanted 
her to get involved with us Twilights.

00:20:31.550 --> 00:20:37.240
Well, I wish her all the 
best with her school life.

00:22:10.760 --> 00:22:11.810
This is it.

00:22:13.640 --> 00:22:17.540
This is where our new life begins.

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:20.630
401, 401...

00:22:20.630 --> 00:22:21.320
Found it.

00:22:21.320 --> 00:22:23.190
Sorry I'm late, Shinyao.

00:22:26.580 --> 00:22:27.280
Shinyao!

00:22:35.260 --> 00:23:32.070
<b>Phantom Twilight 
Plus</b>

00:22:35.680 --> 00:22:37.170
Phantom in the Twilight Plus!

00:22:38.750 --> 00:22:42.860
In the first episode, we'll introduce you 
to this person who holds the key to the story.

00:22:42.860 --> 00:22:44.040
I'm Baileu Ton.

00:22:44.040 --> 00:22:47.280
I moved from China to my beloved London.

00:22:47.280 --> 00:22:51.500
Ton's great-grandmother 
used to live here long ago.

00:22:51.500 --> 00:22:52.320
That's right.

00:22:52.320 --> 00:22:53.820
Her name was Sha Rijan.

00:22:53.820 --> 00:22:57.140
She was a legendary career woman
 who made a name for herself in London

00:22:57.140 --> 00:22:58.660
about a hundred years ago.

00:22:58.660 --> 00:23:01.000
She doesn't have a good 
reputation back home, though.

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:01.960
That's right.

00:23:01.960 --> 00:23:04.490
Because she left her newborn child,

00:23:04.490 --> 00:23:06.960
they call her a traitor 
who abandoned her family.

00:23:06.960 --> 00:23:09.800
I'm sure she had a good reason for it.

00:23:09.800 --> 00:23:11.420
Yeah, I'm sure she did.

00:23:11.420 --> 00:23:15.640
After all, even after moving to London, 
she sent countless letters back home.

00:23:15.640 --> 00:23:17.420
What was written in them?

00:23:17.780 --> 00:23:21.410
Magic spells and patterns?

00:23:21.410 --> 00:23:23.740
Was she a fortune teller?

00:23:23.740 --> 00:23:25.570
It's not important.

00:23:25.570 --> 00:23:28.070
Next time we'll introduce you to Shinyao.

00:23:28.070 --> 00:23:30.430
Oh, I'm going to be kidnapped for a while.

00:23:30.430 --> 00:23:31.620
That'll have to wait.

00:23:31.620 --> 00:23:34.030
What?!

00:23:34.990 --> 00:23:50.010
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:35.110 --> 00:23:36.700
I've always wanted to visit London.

00:23:36.700 --> 00:23:40.750
The moment I arrived, I was robbed 
and my friend vanished in this dangerous city!

00:23:40.750 --> 00:23:42.240
What am I supposed to do now?

00:23:42.240 --> 00:23:43.530
There's no one I can rely—

00:23:43.530 --> 00:23:46.920
Wait, wasn't there that 
pretentious and creepy guy?

00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:50.480
<b>Episode 2 Shadows Who Fight Shadows</b>

00:23:47.250 --> 00:23:50.010
Next time: "Shadows Who Fight Shadows."
